Develop a plan for a task or project that includes:
- a brief description of the task or project;
- the purpose or goal;
- the desired outcome;
- the target audience; and,
- the optimal format of the finished product.

Demonstrate a logical problem solving approach when difficulties arise while carrying out a task:
- Identify the problem;
- Consider or brainstorm solutions;
- Assess possible options;
- Choose a solution; and,
- Implement the solution.

Use the following to perform an advanced internet search:
- a search engine’s built-in advanced search features (e.g., exact word or phrase, language, site or domain);
- logical (Boolean) operators (e.g., AND, OR, NOT);
- search operators such as “ ” (for exact phrase), - (to remove a word), and site: (to search within a site or domain).

Investigate a specific application of AI (e.g., spam filters):
- Describe the purpose of the AI application (e.g., to detect and prevent the delivery of unwanted email);
- Present or illustrate a specific example of the application (e.g., show the feature in one’s email inbox);
- Explain how the application is an example of AI (e.g., it learns from, and makes judgments based on, certain criteria); and,
- Evaluate the effectiveness of the AI application (e.g., It reduces the amount of junk, but it might also filter important email).

Apply basic cell and document formatting features such as:
- changing font attributes (e.g., size, style, colour, underline, bold, italics);
- changing cell attributes (e.g., number category, alignment, fill, borders);
- adding or removing headers and footers; and,
- changing the page layout (e.g., margins, orientation, paper size).

Edit simple spreadsheets by:
- making corrections;
- applying the text to columns function;
- inserting and deleting rows or columns;
- combining multiple columns into one;
- moving and copying formulas, rows and columns; and,
- performing calculations and recalculations.

Query a specific database in order to display records that meet given criteria, following steps such as:
- Filter and search records;
- Construct and use select, parameter and action queries;
- Add a calculated field to a query;
- Perform calculations on a record grouping;
- Design and produce reports to generate results as specified; and,
- Format a report for printing.

Create forms to a specified design and layout:
- create forms and subforms;
- control data entry through forms;
- create calculated fields; and,
- add appropriate controls in forms.

Plan for the development of a relational database:
- determine the purpose of the database;
- consider the most effective organization of the database;
- anticipate the necessary data to include in the database; and,
- identify the end-user of the database.

Establish a vision for the production of a 3 to 5-minute video, considering:
- objectives (e.g., to sell a product);
- theme or genre (e.g., persuasive);
- message or story (e.g., this is the best product for…); and,
- target audience (e.g., clients).

Develop a project plan that includes:
- project timeline;
- equipment;
- set design;
- props;
- other necessary resources;
- shooting location(s);
- special permissions;
- production and editing software, hardware or applications; and,
- presentation method and tools.

Discuss the following considerations in relation to the posting of digital content:
- copyright;
- digital responsibilities;
- ethical considerations; and,
- one’s digital footprint.

Showcase an interest, skill or accomplishment such as:
- technology (e.g., document production, data analysis, photography, video production, animation, website design);
- academics (e.g., language arts, social sciences, physical sciences, math);
- sports (e.g., school sports, community sports, personal activities);
- clubs (e.g., student council, Gay-Straight Alliance, Model United Nations, Students Against Drunk Driving);
- arts (e.g., drawing, painting, music, dance); and,
- trades (e.g., welding, automotive, carpentry, agriculture).

Develop a procedural guide for the work placement that includes items such as:
