- segregation which occurs when one population exists apart from another population so that contact and sharing of cultures does not readily occur;
- assimilation which occurs when a less powerful culture is merged with another dominant culture so that the identity of the assimilated culture is lost; and
- annihilation which occurs when the culture of a weaker society is destroyed by the culture of a more powerful society.

